In 2021, measures were intensified within the GRENKE Group to implement the regulatory requirements for sustainability risks as part of risk management.In the course of the gradual integration of sustainability risks into risk management, sustainability risks, among others, were taken into consideration as part of the risk inventory.Sustainability risks, in particular, should not be seen as a separate new type of risk, but as driving forces that will materialise in the types of risk already known.We have taken sustainability risks into account qualitatively in the risk inventory by analysing physical risks (e.g.extreme weather events) and transitory risks (e.g.change in customer preference in response to climate change or environmental pollution) to determine the extent to which they influence the existing risk types.

